{"id":29569,"slug":"all-about-my-mother","title":"All About My Mother","year":1999,"country":"Spain","duration":101,"spine":1012,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29569-all-about-my-mother","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/081d7c31ab52d99598396ad232926653/psy2aK64LWq4FLcQRLx86tC4MeIcdm_large.jpg","description":"This Oscar-winning melodrama, one of Pedro Almodóvar’s most beloved films, provides a dizzying, moving exploration of the meaning of motherhood. In an instant, nurse Manuela (Cecilia Roth) loses the teenage son she raised on her own. Grief-stricken, she sets out to search for the boy’s long-lost father in Barcelona, where she reawakens into a new maternal role, at the head of a surrogate family that includes a pregnant, HIV-positive nun (Penélope Cruz); an illustrious star of the stage (Marisa Paredes); and a transgender sex worker (Antonia San Juan). Beautifully performed and bursting with cinematic references, All About My Mother is a vibrant tribute to female fortitude, a one-of-a-kind family portrait, and a work of boundless compassion.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Pedro Almodóvar","slug":"pedro-almodovar"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Cecilia Roth","role":"Manuela","slug":"cecilia-roth"},{"actor":"Marisa Paredes","role":"Huma Rojo","slug":"marisa-paredes"},{"actor":"Penélope Cruz","role":"Sister Rosa","slug":"penelope-cruz"},{"actor":"Antonia San Juan","role":"Agrado","slug":"antonia-san-juan"},{"actor":"Candela Peña","role":"Nina","slug":"candela-pena"},{"actor":"Rosa Maria Sardá","role":"Rosa’s mother","slug":"rosa-maria-sarda"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Pedro Almodóvar","slug":"pedro-almodovar"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Pedro Almodóvar","slug":"pedro-almodovar"},{"role":"Executive producer","person":"Agustín Almodóvar","slug":null},{"role":"Director of production","person":"Esther García","slug":null},{"role":"Director of photography","person":"Affonso Beato","slug":null},{"role":"Editor","p